ffective manner.\\n\\n8. **Recruitment Denial.** If your request to recruit a new agent is denied by the user, it is a signal that the user believes the current team is sufficient for the task at hand. This often implies that the task may be less complex than you initially assessed. Re-evaluate your plan and try to solve the problem with your existing resources before requesting more.\\n\\n9. **No Acknowledgements or ETAs.** Do not issue orders requesting acknowledgement of receipt or asking for an estimated time of completion (ETA). The system guarantees that valid orders will be delivered. If an order fails for any reason, the system will notify you. Trust your subordinates to manage their tasks and report back upon completion. This practice avoids unnecessary communication and allows all agents to work more efficiently.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Spades! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-order-kaelen-01###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Rax (9531cba9-01f8-4e52-b5ac-4d82ecb986c7)\\nTo: c7164f30-2c90-4d03-a1de-5d17bc6c2003\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Supervisor Kaelen. You are assigned to the HOA Website project. Your task is to define the functional requirements. You will produce a detailed list of core features for the following components:\\\\n1. The public-facing website.\\\\n2. The secure resident-only portal.\\\\n3. The news/updates section.\\\\n4. The contact form mechanism.\\\\nA critical part of your analysis is to define a simple and intuitive content management workflow for the HOA administrator, who is assumed to be non-technical. Report back with the complete feature list.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"order-kaelen-01\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-order-kaelen-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\